# Build context for the all-in-one Render image (api-gateway/Dockerfile.render).
#
# The context is the repository root because the image needs both the frontend and the gateway.
# Excluding the host's build outputs keeps the context small and, more importantly, stops a
# Windows-generated lockfile from breaking the Linux build: such a lockfile records win32-only
# native binaries (for example `@rolldown/binding-win32-x64-msvc`) and npm aborts with
# EBADPLATFORM when asked to install them on Linux.

**/node_modules

**/package-lock.json
npm-debug.log*

**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
.nyc_output

# Local secrets must never be baked into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!**/.env.example

.git
.gitignore
.github
**/*.md

**/data/*.json
**/uploads

# Tests, tooling and documentation are not needed to build or run the service.
api-gateway/test
sandbox
tools
docs
demo
database

# NOTE: `genai-hub` is deliberately NOT excluded. The all-in-one image compiles the hub and
# copies its Python AST parser, so the directory must stay in the build context. Its own
# node_modules and dist are already covered by the patterns above.
genai-hub/test
